      "info": {
        "contact": {
          "email": "hello@brontie.ie",
          "name": "Kevin Honer, Brontie"
        },
        "description": "Partners call this API to issue a Brontie voucher. We return a redemption\nlink. The partner surfaces that link inside their own product. Brontie does\nnot contact the recipient: no email, no SMS.\n\nThe recipient chooses a partner cafe themselves after receiving the link,\nnot at issue time, so no cafe is associated with a voucher until the\nrecipient picks one.\n\nMoney comes off a balance topped up in advance. There is no refund path back\nto the balance, including for vouchers that are never redeemed.\n\nSelf-service top-up is still being built. Until it ships, balances are\ncredited by arrangement with Brontie.\n\nScope: Republic of Ireland, EUR only.\n\nRead the Idempotency section before building. The `idempotencyKey` is\nrequired and the retry behaviour around it is the only surprising part of\nthis API.\n",
        "security": {
          "in": "header",
          "name": "Authorization",
          "prefix": "Bearer",
          "scheme": "bearerAuth",
          "type": "http"
        },
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production. Key prefix determines live or test mode.",
            "url": "https://www.brontie.ie"
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Issue coffee vouchers against a pre-funded balance.",
        "title": "Brontie Partner API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "website": "https://brontie.ie",
        "x-status": "Voucher issuing, balance and outbound webhooks (voucher.created, voucher.redeemed, balance.low) are all live. Reconciliation endpoints, simulate-redemption, self-service top-up and low-balance alert *emails* (to Brontie, distinct from the balance.low webhook to the partner) are not yet built."
      },
